File Index

/LayoutShellProps.ts
Purpose: HudShellBaseProps — the props contract every theme's shell component receives from MainContainer (isConnected, sendRaw, autoleveling callbacks/state, terminalSlotRef). Each shell sources anything else it needs (sizing, resize handles, sub-components) internally via its own hooks, so every entry in features/hudLayout/themeRegistry.ts's THEME_REGISTRY can be swapped through this one uniform interface. terminalSlotRef is a ref callback the shell attaches to a bare div where its own <Terminal/> would have gone — MainContainer.tsx portals the single, real <Terminal/> instance there, so a live theme switch never remounts it (and loses scrollback).

/DefaultThemeShell.tsx
Purpose: The 'default' theme's registry entry. Thin adapter around the classic LayoutShell — calls useLayoutSizing() itself and supplies BottomPaneComponent, so LayoutShell's historically prop-driven sizing is hidden behind HudShellBaseProps like every other theme's shell.

/CompactLayoutShell.tsx
Purpose: The 'slate-amber' theme's registry entry for DESKTOP widths (features/hudLayout/themeRegistry.ts's ShellComponent; below its 900px narrowBreakpoint, resolveActiveTheme picks CompactLayoutShellNarrow.tsx instead — see that file). Left column: bordered terminal panel (title = character name, via useCharacterIdentity) rendering a bare div via terminalSlotRef (MainContainer.tsx portals the hoisted <Terminal/> in, not this component directly), then CompactVitalsRow/CompactRoomRow/the hud.bottomStrip widget slot/CommandInput. Right column: ChatPane, then AffectsBlock (wrapped in a plain `sa-hud-affects-panel` div so the theme CSS has a stable hook instead of matching AffectsBlock's Vite-hashed class name) and the hud.rightColumn widget slot. Sizing (resizer drag, CSS custom properties) comes from useCompactLayoutSizing. Footer label is a fixed "Slate & Amber" constant — this component only ever represents that one theme. Directly imports styles/hud/themes/slateAmber.theme.scss (side-effect) so that CSS bundles into this component's own lazy chunk.

/CompactLayoutShellNarrow.tsx
Purpose: The 'slate-amber' theme's OWN narrow-viewport shell (features/hudLayout/themeRegistry.ts's NarrowShellComponent for this theme; resolveActiveTheme picks this at/below the 900px breakpoint instead of falling back to DefaultThemeShell). Single column: terminal panel, CompactVitalsRow, CompactRoomRow, the hud.bottomStrip widget slot, CommandInput, then a Chat/Affects tab strip (own local useState, not useBottomPane — different tab set; no separate Compass tab since exits already show inline in CompactRoomRow) — mirrors classic LayoutShell's own narrow-width pattern (stack + tab away secondary content, see LayoutShell.module.scss's @media (max-width: 900px) + BottomPane) rather than a new responsive idiom. No resizer/sizing hook at all — single column has nothing to divide. Also imports slateAmber.theme.scss directly (a phone-width-only session must get the theme CSS bundled into ITS chunk, can't assume the desktop shell's chunk loaded first).

/CompactVitalsRow.tsx
Purpose: HP/Mana/MOVE gauges (useStatusBlockViewModel), a conditional EXP gauge (useLevelProgress — hidden at max level 51 or until level and tnl are known; percent value, exact level/exp-to-level in a tooltip; fill class sa-hud-vitals-fill-exp) plus the enemy gauge (useOpponentStatus, only rendered while isEnemyActive). Each fill element carries a plain sa-hud-vitals-fill-{hp,mp,move,exp,enemy} class alongside its CSS-module class — the module supplies the default color, a theme may override it. The enemy label is rendered via ansiToHtml (dangerouslySetInnerHTML) — mirrors RightSidebar's classic-layout treatment so a color-coded mob name (probe-opponent-condition.ts deliberately keeps the label's raw ANSI) renders identically in both themes instead of showing as plain text.

/CompactRoomRow.tsx
Purpose: Room name + bracketed available-exits row (useRoomHeader, useCompassBlock). Exit buttons call move(dir) on click.

/CompactWidgetSlot.tsx
Purpose: Renders whatever a plugin has published (via PluginRuntimeApi.setHudWidget) into a given HudSlotId, or nothing if the slot is empty. Reads the current occupant from hudWidgetRegistry on mount and re-syncs on HUD_WIDGET_UPDATED_EVENT; its ListenEvent key is suffixed with useId() so multiple instances of the same slotId don't evict each other's listener registration.
